### Describe the bug

- Followup edge cases for https://github.com/swc-project/swc/issues/2549, https://github.com/swc-project/swc/issues/2606

When an function is async, default exported it does not reassign its ref to export as similar to original #2549 does.

### Input code

```typescript
export default function someCall() {
  region();
}

export const text = {};
Object.defineProperty(test, 'someCall', {
  set: (v) => {
    someCall = v;
  }
})
```


### Config

```json
{
  "jsc": {
    "target": "es2017"
  },
  "module": {
    "type": "commonjs",
    "noInterop": false
  },
  "env": {
    "targets": {
      "node": 14
    },
    "include": ["transform-async-to-generator"]
  }
}
```


### Playground link

https://play.swc.rs/?version=1.2.106&code=H4sIAAAAAAAAAz2NQQrCMBBF94Hc4e%2BaQPEAlrrxAHqFGqdSiUlJpqVScndHgm7f579H2xwT407jsHjGuATHUwzI8UXnwXtjsWsFJHoINrbTqmilFdWfiyEzmDZGj73Ierk9yfFBhFOga4ozJX4bpswtmp%2B1aas1Ex9hVov%2BVAH%2BYfGt3RdJrtgP6sRtQKcAAAA%3D&config=H4sIAAAAAAAAA0WNSwrDMAxE76J1Fm2hXeQOPYRxleDgHxoFGozvXju4ZCfNPD0V2mBpLpSNgKVPOKKaL82kR2ZYcVlpIkWLFuPBtS1GVtaGMB63%2B7PVPiXwACYKLrrl6DKbQhYGrsrE1f%2FJ2lwhffYelPPf6XxRvRzjzuE9QJWd6w%2ByirtzuAAAAA%3D%3D

### Expected behavior

Same as #2549, #2606, expect to get reassign like 

```
  set: (v) => {
	exports.someCall = someCall = v;
  }

```

### Version

1.2.106 (and potentially master TOT)

### Additional context

- Looks like potentially related to https://github.com/swc-project/swc/issues/2677 , but for now separating issue until we can triage if it shares same root cause.

